1 NAME Derbforgaill (Dervorgilla) /O'NÇill/
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1108
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1193
1 NOTE She was the subject of the colouful episode of Irish History known as the Rape of Dervorgila. The beautiful Dervorgilla was the lover of the passionate Dermot King of Leinster. She married Tiernan O'Rourke (one-eyed). In 1152 Dermot was at war wit
2 CONC h Tiernan so he attackjed and carried off his wife (not unwillingly). She was taken back a year later by the High King Turlough O'connor. Within a year she was confined to the convent of Clonmacniose and nothing more was heard of her.
